it is not uncommon for servers to get less than the standard minimum wage, but how much less varies from one state to the next. The states where servers are paid the smallest amount are the states where people tip higher percentages. That's the major driver of differences in tipping, although I've done some research showing, for example, that in coffee shop, states where people score higher on kindness tend to tip more. Let's talk for a minute about tip creep. In the last few years, those digital payment screens are popping up everywhere, even at self-service kiosks. Have they changed the norms around tipping and are we now expected to tip in situations where we weren't in the past? Yes, we are expected to tip in situations where we weren't

